<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.4.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01308</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.4.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>399a79e5-86ab-447c-ab5f-1d605f2e7fad</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="a4b3df1e-787b-4380-9bea-e052f15d2675" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which expression is equal to \(4^0\cdot 4^2\)? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>0</para>
            <para>1</para>
            <para>16</para>
            <para>64</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.2.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 16. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="0bfb4b3e-7996-4284-a129-89b0f79266ff" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para><emphasis>Select three </emphasis>expressions that are equivalent to \(3^8\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.1.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac{3^{10}}{3^2}\), \(\left(3^4\right)^2\), \(\left(3\cdot3\right)^4\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="8217780b-cc22-4080-89a5-6eb722331b06" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For 3 - 6 use the following table:</para>
            <para>
              <quote>An investment bond is initially bought for $250. It doubles in value every decade. For each of the missing spaces in the table, a–d, select the missing value that helps complete the table.</quote>
            </para>
            <para>The dollar value of the bond, 0 decades</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is $250.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="ed13f0be-b6d2-4248-b7b7-4f4de2869ec9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The dollar value of the bond, 1 decade</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is $500.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="28f93dea-534f-417c-9a03-03d889af215c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The dollar value of the bond, 2 decades</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is $1,000.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="d90e4d30-5f4f-4a37-9db9-adbe0138fda2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The dollar value of the bond, 3 decades</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is $2,000.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="92cb5906-4754-4d01-bfe0-8e2dcc47c7a1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>An investment bond is initially bought for $250. It doubles in value every decade. How many decades does it take before the bond is worth more than $10,000?
          <emphasis> </emphasis>
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.4.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 6.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="ecb5e1c2-e194-4527-a10d-fe2ece40c6f4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>An investment bond is initially bought for $250. It doubles in value every decade. Choose an equation that relates \(V\), the value of the bond, to \(d\), the number of decades since the bond was bought.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(V = 250\cdot d^2\)</para>
            <para>\(V = 500^d\)</para>
            <para>\(V = 250\cdot 2\cdot d\)</para>
            <para>\(V = 250\cdot 2^d\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.4.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(V = 250\cdot 2^d\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="602114a2-6812-4d50-ac86-abf520e824f7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A sea turtle population \(p\) is modeled by the equation \(p=400\cdot(1.25)^y\) where \(y\) is the number of years since the population was first measured. How many turtles are in the population when it is first measured? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.5.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 400.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="befadee8-0d0a-4180-841a-c64efb4bcd0e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A sea turtle population \(p\) is modeled by the equation \(p=400\cdot(1.25)^y\) where \(y\) is the number of years since the population was first measured. After how many years will the turtle population reach 700? Round to the nearest full year. <emphasis> </emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.5.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 2.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="f1c4dd95-dbd4-48cb-96bc-51a8da17ade4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following information to answer questions 11 and 12.</para>
            <newline/>
            <para>Which account has more money after one week? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is Bank Account B.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="aaba644a-2de8-49da-b103-d5590f6e3b68" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which account has more money after fifteen weeks?
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.4
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is Bank Account A.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="cfb66877-9a06-47a9-a574-ae7b93143c0f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For 13 - 15, use this graph showing the two account balances.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>
                <figure>
                  <media alt="Graph of 2 discrete lines, origin O, with grid. Number of weeks and amount in dollars.">
                    <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_06_13_01.svg"/>
                  </media>
                </figure>
              </quote>
            </para>
            <para>The graph of the red triangles corresponds to which bank account?
          </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.3.
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is Bank Account A. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="196be8d6-bcb3-4cb6-8881-9a9d61028274" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graph of the blue circles corresponds to which bank account?
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.4
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is Bank Account B.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="baedeabc-d833-4d6f-a783-aec840a78031" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the two accounts would you choose for long-term saving?
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.4.4
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is Bank Account B.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
